// Title: UAC Bypass Using IDiagnostic Profile - File
// Sigma ID: 48ea844d-19b1-4642-944e-fe39c2cc1fec
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-03 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, privilege-escalation, T1548.002
// Description: Detects the creation of a file by "dllhost.exe" in System32 directory part of
//   "IDiagnosticProfileUAC" UAC bypass technique
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/Wh04m1001/IDiagnosticProfileUAC
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_uac_bypass_idiagnostic_profile.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\DllHost.exe" and FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\System32\\" and FolderPath endswith ".dll"
